Bundle the small-surface shell as its own web entry point.

shell.ts is the runtime half of narrow.css and touch.css - the back guard, the
viewport/keyboard custom properties, the modal-editor and keybindings-scroll
behaviours. It used to ship as a hand-written file copied verbatim into the
built output, which put it outside every check the rest of our code gets (no
compiler, no lint, no rebrand) and, worse, left it unable to import anything:
the narrow breakpoint and the touch query were restated in it by hand and held
together only by a mirror test.

As an entry point it is ordinary source in the overlay, imports the two
canonical gates, and is bundled by the same step as the workbench. The
stylesheets still mirror the queries, because CSS cannot import a constant, and
the mirror test still pins those.

Both entry lists get it. The shipped reh-web bundle reads buildfile.ts today,
but upstream is moving to build/next, and a bundle that silently omits this
entry is exactly the failure worth spending a second hunk on: the workbench
still loads, only the whole small-screen shell is missing.

--- a/lib/vscode/build/buildfile.ts
+++ b/lib/vscode/build/buildfile.ts
@@ -50,7 +50,11 @@
 	createModuleDescription('vs/sessions/electron-browser/sessions'),
 ];
 
-export const codeWeb = createModuleDescription('vs/code/browser/workbench/workbench');
+export const codeWeb = [
+	createModuleDescription('vs/code/browser/workbench/workbench'),
+	// Composery: loaded by workbench.html ahead of the workbench entry.
+	createModuleDescription('vs/code/browser/workbench/shell'),
+];
 
 export const codeServer = [
 	// 'vs/server/node/server.main' is not included here because it gets inlined via ./src/server-main.js
--- a/lib/vscode/build/next/index.ts
+++ b/lib/vscode/build/next/index.ts
@@ -117,6 +117,8 @@
 const webEntryPoints = [
 	'vs/workbench/workbench.web.main.internal',
 	'vs/code/browser/workbench/workbench',
+	// Composery: loaded by workbench.html ahead of the workbench entry.
+	'vs/code/browser/workbench/shell',
 ];
 
 // Additional web-only entry points (CDN build only, not in server-web)
